  "worked_solution": "First we plot the graph of $y={(\\frac{1}{6})}^{x}:$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14239148/assets/4dacecba4626f7c202777cad0a723295a2954f4b0c65fde83a81c6c849414d51.png)\n\nThen, we scale this graph by a factor of $2.$ The $y$-intercept becomes $(0,2),$ and the resulting graph is as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14239148/assets/b747ae8c29f01b840930d81f9c4b706d049ca685ee982efff717ddb13213937d.png)",
